{0 KV}

{!Workero.KV} is a
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/}Workers KV} namespace: a global
key-value store with text values.

{1 Configure}

{@sh[
npx wrangler kv namespace create KV
]}

Copy the printed [id] into [wrangler.toml]:

{@toml[
[[kv_namespaces]]
binding = "KV"
id = "<namespace id>"
]}

{1 Use}

{@ocaml[
let handler req env _ctx =
  let open Workero in
  let kv = KV.of_env env "KV" in
  let url = Request.url req in
  let key = Option.value (URL.query url "k") ~default:"" in
  match (Request.method_ req, URL.path url) with
  | GET, "/kv" -> (
      match KV.get kv key with
      | Some value -> Response.text value
      | None -> Response.text ~status:404 "not found\n")
  | PUT, "/kv" ->
      KV.put ~expiration_ttl:3600 kv key (Request.text req);
      Response.text "stored\n"
  | DELETE, "/kv" ->
      KV.delete kv key;
      Response.text "deleted\n"
  | GET, "/keys" ->
      let prefix = URL.query url "prefix" in
      Response.text (String.concat "\n" (KV.list ?prefix kv) ^ "\n")
  | _ -> Response.text ~status:404 "not found\n"

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

- {!Workero.KV.of_env} opens the namespace bound as ["KV"]. It raises
  [Invalid_argument] when there is no such binding.
- {!Workero.KV.get} gives [Some value], or [None] when the key does not exist.
- {!Workero.KV.put} stores a value. [~expiration_ttl] is a number of seconds.
  Cloudflare requires at least 60.
- {!Workero.KV.delete} removes a key. A missing key is not an error.
- {!Workero.KV.list} gives the names of all keys that start with [~prefix], in
  lexicographic order. KV returns at most 1000 keys for each request.
  [list] follows the cursor until the listing is complete, so a large namespace
  takes several requests and its names are all held in memory. It raises
  [Failure "Workero.KV.list: ..."] when KV reports an incomplete page.

Values are text. KV is eventually consistent: a change can take up to 60 seconds
to show in other locations.

{1 Test locally}

{@sh[
npx wrangler dev
curl -X PUT -d hello "localhost:8787/kv?k=greeting"
curl "localhost:8787/kv?k=greeting"
]}
